    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate focusing on high-ceiling matchups against soft-tossing arms. **Corbin Carroll** leads the squad with an elite 80.77 score; despite a minor platoon disadvantage against Abbott, his combination of batting order stability and massive speed upside against a vulnerable pitcher makes him our primary anchor. **Vinnie Pasquantino** follows closely at 76.21, benefiting significantly from a favorable platoon matchup against Waguespack. Similarly, **Gabriel Moreno** projects for a strong 66.77 score, as he capitalizes on a high-value #3 spot in the order and a favorable 5.01 xERA matchup against Abbott, who serves as a primary target for our offense today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Isaac Paredes**, who posted a 45.78 score but ultimately lacked the categorical necessity to crack the starting nine. While **Isaac Paredes** offers a solid floor, the optimizer prioritized the speed-first profile of players like **Brice Turang** and **Henry Bolte**, the latter of whom earns a start thanks to his favorable #1 spot in the order against the hittable Javier. We are managing risks carefully, particularly with **Austin Riley** and **Josh Naylor**, both of whom are facing difficult left-handed arms in Drohan and Imanaga, respectively, which has dampened their projected efficiency. We are also closely monitoring **Mickey Moniak**, whose score of 54.50 remains solid despite a sharp platoon penalty, as his park environment provides enough of a boost to keep him in the lineup over the marginal bench options like **Griffin Conine** or **Cole Young**. With **James Wood** still sidelined on the IL, we are relying on this depth to maintain our standing in the Roto race.",
